---
import PortalLayout from '../layouts/PortalLayout.astro';
---

<PortalLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Terra Chartarum handles analytics, cookies, personal information, and external collection links."
>
  <section class="shell prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1>Read without a profile</h1>
    <p>
      Terra Chartarum is a static publication. It has no reader accounts, comments, advertising
      pixels, behavioural profiles, or forms that collect personal information.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      This site measures aggregate traffic with Cloudflare Web Analytics: how many pages were
      viewed, which ones, which site a visitor arrived from, and a country-level location. It is
      enabled on the hosting platform rather than in the page source, so the measurement script is
      added when the site is served.
    </p>
    <p>
      Cloudflare states that Web Analytics uses no cookies and no other client-side storage for
      analytics, does not fingerprint visitors, and does not track people over time by IP address or
      user-agent string. Referral counts are derived from page views rather than from stored visitor
      identities. See Cloudflare's
      <a href="https://blog.cloudflare.com/privacy-first-web-analytics/"
        >account of how the measurement works</a
      >
      and its <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Because that configuration sets no analytics cookies and stores nothing on your device, this
      site publishes this notice instead of a cookie-consent banner asking permission for storage it
      does not use. If the provider, measurements, storage, or legal context changes, analytics must
      be held until this notice and the consent decision are reviewed again.
    </p>
    <p>
      A second, unused integration for
      <a href="https://plausible.io/privacy-focused-web-analytics">Plausible Analytics</a> remains in
      the site code. It is disabled: no Plausible script is emitted on any page, and enabling it would
      require a new build explicitly configured with a site-specific script.
    </p>

    <h2>External links and media</h2>
    <p>
      Essays link to libraries, archives, map collections, scholarship, and source records.
      Following an external link takes you to another organisation with its own privacy practices.
      The portal's production images and fonts are served from the site itself; a catalogue record
      may preserve an external source URL for attribution without loading it automatically.
    </p>

    <h2>Search engines</h2>
    <p>
      The site is registered with Google Search Console, which reports how often its pages appeared
      in search results and which queries led to them. Those reports are aggregate counts produced
      by the search engine from its own logs; the site neither receives nor stores anything about an
      individual searcher.
    </p>

    <h2>Operational logs</h2>
    <p>
      The hosting provider may process ordinary request and security logs needed to deliver and
      protect the site. Those platform logs are separate from the analytics described above.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      Analytics remains a reversible feature: it can be switched off at the hosting platform, which
      stops the script being served on every page. Material changes to collection or tracking
      require an updated privacy review before release.
    </p>
  </section>
</PortalLayout>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: 72ch;
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
  }
  .prose h1 {
    margin: 0.3rem 0 1.25rem;
    font-size: var(--step-4);
  }
  .prose h2 {
    margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem;
    font-size: var(--step-2);
  }
</style>
